---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/forecasts.css';
---
<Layout title="Forecast journal" description="Every CryptoOracle forecast kept on record: the original prediction, the observed outcome and the evidence for controlled learning.">
  <div class="wrap forecast-page">
    <header class="forecast-hero"><p class="eyebrow">THE FORECAST JOURNAL · LIVE RESEARCH</p><h1>We made a prediction.<br /><em>Did it hold up?</em></h1><p>Each forecast is saved before its target time. When that time arrives, we compare it with the observed price. The original prediction stays on the record.</p><a class="text-link" href="#learning">See how the system learns ↘</a></header>
    <div class="forecast-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"><p id="forecast-status">Loading the public research record…</p><button class="forecast-button" id="refresh-forecasts" type="button">Refresh</button></div>
    <noscript><p>The method below works without JavaScript. Reading the live journal requires JavaScript; the <a href="/api/forecasts">public JSON</a> is also available directly.</p></noscript>
    <section aria-label="Choose forecasts" class="forecast-filters">
      <label>Asset<select id="forecast-asset" aria-label="Asset"><option value="BTC">Bitcoin</option><option value="ETH">Ethereum</option><option value="SOL">Solana</option></select></label>
      <label>Horizon<select id="forecast-horizon" aria-label="Horizon"><option value="24">24 hours</option><option value="72">72 hours</option></select></label>
      <label>Model<select id="forecast-model" aria-label="Model"><option value="timesfm">TimesFM · original</option><option value="calibrated">Learned calibration · shadow</option><option value="fusion_market">Market correction · shadow</option><option value="fusion_news">FinBERT news correction · shadow</option></select></label>
      <label>Show<select id="forecast-filter" aria-label="Show"><option value="scored">Settled forecasts</option><option value="pending">Waiting for target</option><option value="awaiting">Waiting for outcome data</option><option value="all">All forecasts</option></select></label>
    </section>
    <section class="forecast-scores" id="forecast-scores" aria-label="Observed model quality"></section>
    <p class="forecast-caveat" id="forecast-cohort">Scores use the same origins as the persistence baseline. Hourly forecasts overlap; their count is not a count of independent market events.</p>
    <section id="forecast-detail" class="forecast-detail" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Selected forecast" hidden></section>
    <section class="forecast-list-section" aria-labelledby="journal-heading"><div class="forecast-section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">CHOOSE A RECORD TO INSPECT</p><h2 id="journal-heading">Predicted. Observed. Preserved.</h2></div><span id="forecast-count" class="fine-print"></span></div><div id="forecast-list" class="forecast-list"></div><div class="forecast-pagination"><button id="forecast-prev" class="forecast-button" type="button" disabled>← Newer</button><span id="forecast-page-number"></span><button id="forecast-next" class="forecast-button" type="button" disabled>Older →</button></div></section>
    <section class="learning-section" id="learning" aria-labelledby="learning-heading"><p class="eyebrow">CONTROLLED LEARNING</p><h2 id="learning-heading">Learn from settled mistakes.<br /><em>Prove the next change.</em></h2><p>A small correction model learns from earlier TimesFM errors. It predicts alongside the original model, in a separate shadow experiment. It does not control the paper portfolios.</p><div id="learning-state" class="learning-state"><p>Loading the learning stage…</p></div><ol class="learning-steps"><li><b>01 · Freeze</b><p>Save the price target, original reference, model version and information cutoff.</p></li><li><b>02 · Settle</b><p>Wait for the exact target close. Keep the error, even when the direction was right.</p></li><li><b>03 · Check & learn</b><p>Compare outcome prices across three venues. Fit only on earlier, reviewed outcomes.</p></li><li><b>04 · Compare</b><p>Evaluate the candidate on forecasts issued after fitting. Retain the original as a reference.</p></li></ol>
      <details class="forecast-method"><summary>What exactly can change — and when?</summary><p>The calibration candidate learns a regularized correction to past log-price errors. Its endpoint interval comes from a later calibration subset; training targets overlapping that subset are excluded. The interval is expanded to include its point forecast. This is empirical calibration, not guaranteed coverage.</p><p>Fitting requires at least 120 reviewed examples spanning 21 days, plus 60 training and 30 calibration examples after that exclusion. These are minimum data requirements, not proof of quality. A fixed review covers 28 days of future forecast origins after the candidate starts. It checks error against TimesFM, persistence and momentum, interval quality and data availability, using time blocks.</p><p>Reviews produce a recorded verdict. There is no automatic promotion into trading. A supported candidate still requires a separately versioned policy and a future portfolio comparison with the same costs and start conditions.</p><p>The existing FinBERT market/news corrections remain separate. JEV currently classifies headlines and can veto paper buys; it does not numerically revise a price forecast. No future or subsequently collected news is allowed into an earlier prediction.</p></details>
      <details class="forecast-method"><summary>How reliable is the “actual” price?</summary><p>Forecasts target the Binance BTC/USDT, ETH/USDT or SOL/USDT hourly close. Learning labels are checked against Coinbase and Kraken USD closes for the same completed hour, with a same-hour Coinbase USDT/USD close. Converted prices must agree within 1%, and the conversion must remain within 1% of parity.</p><p>Missing references, revised source data or an unverifiable input keep a sample out of the calibration learner. The original score remains visible. A shared market jump can pass these checks; agreement is a plausibility check, not proof that every source is correct. Intermediate observed chart points use the latest stored candle versions; the settled endpoint remains the first recorded evaluation.</p></details>
      <p class="fine-print">Forecast prices are in USDT on Binance. Portfolio returns are in USD and depend on decision-time prices, conversion and trading costs. Forecast accuracy and portfolio profit answer different questions.</p>
    </section>
  </div><script is:inline src="/scripts/forecasts.js" defer></script>
</Layout>
